&lt;h1&gt;Your Mission&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a backend engineer with a focus on Integrations at SPARETECH, you will enable fast and reliable integrations between our platform and our customers’ ERP systems. You will work closely with customer engineering teams (e.g. SAP, middleware, IT) as well as SPARETECH backend engineers, Product, and Customer Success to ensure smooth data exchange via APIs and webhooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine backend engineering expertise with customer-facing collaboration to support integration architecture, implementation, and debugging, helping customers navigate complex and often ambiguous system landscapes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with our Product and Engineering teams to keep evolving our platform beyond integrations and data exchanges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We offer you the opportunity to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a central pillar for successful customer integrations by directly collaborating with (big) enterprise customers and their engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own integration topics end-to-end: from architecture discussions and API usage definition to testing, go-live support, and issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to SPARETECH’s backend (Java/Kotlin) to improve APIs, webhooks, integration reliability as well as the core areas of our web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a fast-paced, collaborative environment across Engineering, Product, and Customer Success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep expertise in enterprise system integration (SAP, middleware, distributed data sync)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex integration problems involving multiple systems, unclear ownership, and real-world constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Become a part of our team if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring 3-7 years of professional software engineering experience, with JVM-based languages (Java, Kotlin, Scala)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience with REST APIs and/or webhooks in distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable debugging issues end-to-end using logs, payloads, and system traces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a solid understanding of data synchronization concepts (e.g. polling, event-driven flows, retries, idempotency)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are familiar with SAP data structures (e.g. IDocs such as MATMAS) and ERP/Middleware architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working with SAP environments (e.g. ECC, S/4HANA), middleware, or enterprise IT landscapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how backend systems interact and can navigate system architectures independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a collaborative approach when working with engineers, product teams, and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are confident communicating technical topics clearly in customer-facing situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of your tasks, deliver reliably, and proactively seek support when neede&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;notion-selectable notion-sub_header-block&quot; data-block-id=&quot;38b618bc-2c80-80ff-bbc5-e58805f066f2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;:r8b:&quot; class=&quot;content-editable-leaf-rtl notranslate&quot; data-content-editable-leaf=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to integration platforms or middleware (e.g. CPI, PI/PO, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating with ERPs other than SAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability tooling, CI/CD, and cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in customer-facing engineering roles or technical support in B2B SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote-yes company, where you can decide every day whether you work from home, at our Stuttgart or Munich office, or at any&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.designoffices.de/&quot;&gt;Design Office&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;in Germany&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A permanent employment contract, 30 days of vacation, and the opportunity to participate in the company&#39;s success through our VSOP program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern hardware and the frame for a height-adjustable desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual training budget of 1000 EURO for your professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Germany: A subsidized&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jobrad.org/&quot;&gt;job bike&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to escape city traffic and a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://qualitrain.net/&quot;&gt;Wellpass&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;gym membership to stay active&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dynamic start-up atmosphere and an international team in which new ideas, creative approaches, and cooperation at eye level are valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To enjoy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.corporate-benefits.de/&quot;&gt;Corporate Benefits&lt;/a&gt;, including discounts on fashion, travel, and much more from various companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SPARETECH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SPARETECH&#39;s vision is to empower the zero-waste industrial sharing economy by enabling maintenance and procurement teams at manufacturing leaders like Bosch, Porsche, and Nestlé to reduce MRO spend and optimize inventory through accurate part information, internal transparency, and market visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To achieve this, we have built, and continue to build, an AI-powered MRO software that connects all players in the spare parts ecosystem, from manufacturers and suppliers to the people working behind the machines. By facilitating the exchange of data, knowledge, and expertise, we create shared visibility that empowers smarter decisions, reduces waste, and drives seamless collaboration. This connected spare parts intelligence unlocks value that extends far beyond software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;https://www.thesaasnews.com/news/sparetech-raises-10-million-in-series-a&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id-1257119756&quot;&gt;Insight Partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, SPARETECH is accelerating its growth with a strong focus on product innovation and team excellence. We take pride in our inclusive and collaborative culture, as well as our energetic and committed team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Purpose of the Position&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As Product Manager, Publisher Payments, you will own and evolve Awin&#39;s global publisher payments experience, ensuring publishers are paid accurately, on time, and through payment methods that best meet their needs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You will shape how Awin delivers seamless payment experiences across countries, currencies and regulatory environments, balancing compliance, operational efficiency and customer experience. You will identify opportunities to simplify payment journeys, improve transparency and trust, and help publishers get paid with confidence, wherever they are in the world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Working closely with product, engineering, finance, support, operations and compliance teams, you will define and deliver solutions that create value for publishers, support business growth and enable Awin to scale its global payments capabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Key Tasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Evolve Awin’s publisher payments experience, ensuring payments are accurate, timely and trusted by publishers across the globe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, prioritize and deliver product initiatives that improve the publisher payments experience, end-to-end &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify payment-related pain points and opportunities through data, customer feedback and market insights, translating them into clear product outcomes &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the evolution of Awin’s global payments capabilities, supporting different countries, currencies, payment methods and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery activities to understand publisher needs, validate assumptions and ensure solutions solve genuine customer problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, customer insights and business context to prioritize opportunities, measure impact and continuously improve payment performance and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across product, engineering, finance and operations to align on priorities and deliver improvements to the publisher payments experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance, Operations, Compliance and Engineering teams to deliver payment solutions that balance customer experience, regulatory requirements and operational efficiency.&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Expertise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;3+ years of experience in product management, preferably in a SaaS environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
